    silm:hasAdditionalAttribute "circuit_corner:2" ;
    silm:hasAdditionalAttribute "dunbar_layer:0" ;
    silm:hasAdditionalAttribute "paper_kind:urn:silmaril:entity#papers.01_orientation" ;
    silm:hasLongDescription "The TypedLegMeasurement is TypedLeg is the third node of the Kleisli pipeline, produced by type^Kl. For the measurement-leg run, TypedLeg instantiates to TypedLeg_measurement: a named olog object representing the MeasurementEvent2024 sort applied to the Mittens 4.1kg reading. Its outgoing arrow is the cocone leg lambda_meas: TypedLeg_measurement -> Mittens that glue^Kl will commit to the colimit." .

silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_14_kleisli_enrichment_pipeline_sections_01_kleisli_category_overview_concrete_anchor_5
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "KleisliOverviewAnchorProfile" ;
    rdfs:label "KleisliOverviewAnchorProfileExample" ;
    silm:hasExample "In 'KleisliOverviewAnchorProfile', the bare-symbol→anchor table grounds the abstract symbols in the Tartu-Animal-Clinic / Mittens-2026-05-18 domain story. For example, Profile is the terminal node of the four-step Kleisli pipeline, produced by profile^Kl. For Mittens it instantiates to the pair (Y^in_Mittens, Y^out_Mittens): the incoming hom-functor Hom(-, Mittens) and outgoing hom-functor Hom(Mittens, -). The profile encodes every typed arrow into Mittens (record, identifier, quality, measurement, role, process, validation, trace, classification, taxonomy legs) and every typed arrow out of Mittens (classification target DomesticCat, derived facts, audit traces). Downstream papers inherit Mittens through this profile; the Yoneda lemma guarantees this fixes Mittens up to isomorphism.." .

silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_14_kleisli_enrichment_pipeline_sections_01_kleisli_category_overview_concrete_anchor_5%23mittensyonedaprofile
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "KleisliOverviewAnchorProfileAddlBaseTopic" ;
    rdfs:label "KleisliOverviewAnchorProfileAddlCircuitCorner" ;
    rdfs:label "KleisliOverviewAnchorProfileAddlDunbarLayer" ;
    rdfs:label "KleisliOverviewAnchorProfileAddlPaperKind" ;
    rdfs:label "urn:silmaril:entity#instances.papers.01_orientation.chapters.14_kleisli_enrichment_pipeline.sections.01_kleisli_category_overview.concrete_anchor_5#mittensyonedaprofile" ;
    silm:hasAdditionalAttribute "base_topic:free monad" ;
    silm:hasAdditionalAttribute "circuit_corner:3" ;
    silm:hasAdditionalAttribute "dunbar_layer:0" ;
    silm:hasAdditionalAttribute "paper_kind:urn:silmaril:entity#papers.01_orientation" ;
    silm:hasLongDescription "The MittensYonedaProfile is Profile is the terminal node of the four-step Kleisli pipeline, produced by profile^Kl. For Mittens it instantiates to the pair (Y^in_Mittens, Y^out_Mittens): the incoming hom-functor Hom(-, Mittens) and outgoing hom-functor Hom(Mittens, -). The profile encodes every typed arrow into Mittens (record, identifier, quality, measurement, role, process, validation, trace, classification, taxonomy legs) and every typed arrow out of Mittens (classification target DomesticCat, derived facts, audit traces). Downstream papers inherit Mittens through this profile; the Yoneda lemma guarantees this fixes Mittens up to isomorphism." .

silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_14_kleisli_enrichment_pipeline_sections_01_kleisli_category_overview_decomposition_step_1__step_g_o%5Ekl_f_%3D_mu_c_o_freesigmag_o_f
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Kleisli composition of f: A -> Free(Sigma)(B) and g: B -> Free(Sigma)(C) is: apply f, then lift g along the monad functor Free(Sigma), then flatten with mu_C. The result is a new Kleisli arrow from A to C." .

silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_14_kleisli_enrichment_pipeline_sections_01_kleisli_category_overview_decomposition_step_2__step_mu_c__freesigmafreesigmac__%3E_freesigmac
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "mu_C is the monad multiplication (flattening): it takes a nested free-monad term Free(Sigma)(Free(Sigma)(C)) and collapses it to a single-level term Free(Sigma)(C). This is the bind-flattening that makes Kleisli composition associative." .

silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_14_kleisli_enrichment_pipeline_sections_01_kleisli_category_overview_decomposition_step_3__step_joc_%C2%A720_1__kleisli_category_klt%3B_identity_is_eta%3B_compositio
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Joy of Cats §20.1 defines the Kleisli category of a monad T: objects are the same as the base category; a Kleisli arrow from A to B is a morphism A -> T(B); the identity Kleisli arrow at A is eta_A; Kleisli composition is mu_C o T(g) o f." .

silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_14_kleisli_enrichment_pipeline_sections_01_kleisli_category_overview_decomposition_step_4__step_measurementevent2024_kleisli_chain__citemittensvetrecord77_b
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "The measurement leg Kleisli chain: cite(mittensVetRecord77) produces Free(Sigma)(Witness_measurement); type binds it to TypedLeg_measurement; glue contributes the leg to the cocone, producing Mittens when all ten legs are present. Kleisli associativity guarantees that regrouping does not change Mittens." .

silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_14_kleisli_enrichment_pipeline_sections_01_kleisli_category_overview_decomposition_step_5__step_kl_embedding_is_full_and_faithful_joc_%C2%A720_1%3B_profile_of_mitt
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "By Yoneda, the profile of the final term in Kl(Free(Sigma)) determines which claims the term supports. The profile of Mittens in Kl(Free(Sigma)) is the same as the profile in O_01 because the Kleisli embedding is full and faithful (JoC §20.1). Every incoming arrow in O_01 corresponds to a Kleisli arrow in Kl(Free(Sigma))." .

silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_14_kleisli_enrichment_pipeline_sections_01_kleisli_category_overview_decomposition_step_6__step_the_publication_pipeline_is_kleisli_composition_in_klfreesigma
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Each bind step in the pipeline is one Kleisli arrow; the whole chain is associative by the monad axioms; the encyclopedia is precisely this Kleisli category with Mittens as its canonical apex." .

