    silm:hasLongDescription "The VerbatimQuoteForJoC620 is VerbatimQuote is the third node in the witness provenance chain — the byte-exact text extracted from the source file. For the joc620 witness, the verbatim quote is \"Natural transformations from the representable functor Hom(-, A) to a set-valued functor F are in natural bijection with the elements of F(A)\" (the Yoneda lemma corollary at JoC §6.20). Source-integrity discipline forbids paraphrase: the field must contain the unmodified text, with omissions visibly marked. Re-citing the same range against the same path must always reproduce the same verbatim quote." .

