    silm:hasAdditionalAttribute "paper_kind:urn:silmaril:entity#papers.01_orientation" ;
    silm:hasLongDescription "The CitekeyAdamekHerrlichStrecker1990JoyOfCats is LocalWitnessKey is the fourth node in the chain. For the joc620 witness, the local citation key is AdamekHerrlichStrecker1990JoyOfCats — the BibLaTeX entry pointing at the Joy of Cats monograph (1990 Wiley, freely redistributed in 2004). The key is the stable identifier that the cite Kleisli arrow uses to track provenance through the encyclopedia. A different witness from the same source (e.g., JoC §11.3 on universal property) reuses the same citekey but a different line range and verbatim quote." .

silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_15_witness_traceability_sections_01_what_is_a_witness_decomposition_step_1__step_w_%3D_pathw__linesw__quotew__keyw
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "A witness object w has four named fields: path(w) is the file path on disk; lines(w) is the line range in that file; quote(w) is the verbatim copied text from those lines; key(w) is the local citation key assigned to this witness. All four must be present for the witness to be traceable." .

silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_15_witness_traceability_sections_01_what_is_a_witness_decomposition_step_2__step_cite__assigns_local_key_and_wraps_as_freesigma_term%3B_type__a
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "The cite Kleisli arrow takes the local key and wraps the witness as a free-monad term in Kl(Free(Sigma)). The type Kleisli arrow then assigns the witness an olog sort from O_01. These are the two operations that transform a raw source fact into a typed load-bearing claim." .

silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_15_witness_traceability_sections_01_what_is_a_witness_decomposition_step_3__step_per_paper_ripper_%C2%A73_witnesses_schema__witness_path__witness_
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "The per-paper-ripper contract section 3 says: every witnesses ledger row must have three fields that constitute the traceability chain: witness_path (file on disk), witness_line_range (specific lines), and verbatim_quote (exact text copied). These three fields map directly to the three of the four witness object fields path(w), lines(w), quote(w). The fourth field key(w) is added by the cite step." .

silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_15_witness_traceability_sections_01_what_is_a_witness_decomposition_step_4__step_joc620_witness__path%3Dcannon_cat_joy_of_cats_md__lines%3D2340_2
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "The joc620 witness is the concrete instantiation of all four fields: path points to the cannon file for Joy of Cats; lines 2340-2360 is the Yoneda lemma corollary; the verbatim quote is the exact text; the local key is the BibTeX key. This witness supports the Kleisli composition theorem via the Yoneda bijection step." .

silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_15_witness_traceability_sections_01_what_is_a_witness_decomposition_step_5__step_y%5Einjoc620_%3D_locate_from_cannon_cat_joy_of_cats_md%3B_y%5Eoutjoc
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "The Yoneda profile of witness joc620 has one incoming arrow (locate from the source file on disk) and two outgoing arrows (one to the Kleisli composition theorem, one to the enrichment section). A witness with no outgoing arrows is an isolated source fact that supports no claim; it exists in the olog but has no effect on the colimit." .

silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_15_witness_traceability_sections_01_what_is_a_witness_decomposition_step_6__step_witness_holds__typed_source_object_with_four_fields
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "A witness is a typed source object with four declared fields (path, lines, quote, key); its Yoneda profile is the set of claims it supports; a witness with no outgoing arrows is isolated and supports no claim." .

