    silm:hasLongDescription "The MittensEnrichmentCenter is Mittens occupies the center column of both rows in the enrichment diagram, instantiated as the running cat: Mrs Hendersons silver-furred domestic cat carrying veterinary record 77 (visit 2024-11-01), microchip ID 2018, weighed 4.1kg. Each adjacent typed hom-set Hom_O_01(X, Mittens) and Hom_O_01(Mittens, Y) carries exactly the named typed arrow shown in the figure; each hom-set is small and explicitly enumerated, illustrating the Set-enrichment property." .

silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_14_kleisli_enrichment_pipeline_sections_02_enrichment_by_type_information_concrete_anchor_4
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "EnrichmentAnchorDomesticCat" ;
    rdfs:label "EnrichmentAnchorDomesticCatExample" ;
    silm:hasExample "In 'EnrichmentAnchorDomesticCat', the bare-symbol→anchor table grounds the abstract symbols in the Tartu-Animal-Clinic / Mittens-2026-05-18 domain story. For example, DomesticCat is the classification sort: a typed olog node whose only incoming hom-set from Mittens is the singleton {lambda_cls}. For the running fixture the membership statement reads \"Mittens is a DomesticCat\"; the enrichment guarantees that no other arrow Mittens -> DomesticCat is admitted unless explicitly added to the olog. DomesticCat is the species-classification leg, NOT identical to Mittens (no isomorphism) and NOT the taxonomy row TaxRow_TSN183798 — they sit on opposite sides of the apex.." .

