silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_14_kleisli_enrichment_pipeline_sections_02_enrichment_by_type_information_decomposition_step_1__step_hom_o_01a_b_in_set_set_enriched_category
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "A Set-enriched category replaces each hom-set with a set object in Set and requires composition to be a function of sets. The page olog O_01 is Set-enriched: every hom-set is a finite set of typed arrows." .

silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_14_kleisli_enrichment_pipeline_sections_02_enrichment_by_type_information_decomposition_step_2__step_sortso_01__witness__typedleg__apex__profile_____%3B_typed_arro
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "The orientation page olog O_01 has explicitly enumerated sorts (Witness, TypedLeg, Apex, Profile, DomesticCat, TaxRow, etc.) and typed arrows with declared domain and codomain. Each hom-set is a finite set of typed arrows; the set is determined by the olog definition." .

silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_14_kleisli_enrichment_pipeline_sections_02_enrichment_by_type_information_decomposition_step_3__step_joc_%C2%A76_18__hom__a_is_contravariant%3B_homa___is_covariant%3B_bot
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "JoC §6.18 defines representable functors: Hom(-,A) is a contravariant Set-valued functor (it assigns to each X the hom-set Hom(X,A)). For Set-enriched categories this is exactly the enriched representable functor." .

silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_14_kleisli_enrichment_pipeline_sections_02_enrichment_by_type_information_decomposition_step_4__step_homvetrecord77__mittens_%3D_about%3B_hommittens__domesticcat_%3D_l
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Hom(VetRecord77, Mittens) is the set containing the single \"about\" arrow: the vet record is about Mittens. Hom(Mittens, DomesticCat) is the set containing the classification arrow lambda_cls. Each hom-set is small and named." .

silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_14_kleisli_enrichment_pipeline_sections_02_enrichment_by_type_information_decomposition_step_5__step_yoneda_for_set_enriched__knowing_all_homx__mittens_uniquely_
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "By the Yoneda lemma for Set-enriched categories, knowing all hom-sets Hom(X, Mittens) for all objects X in O_01 uniquely determines Mittens up to isomorphism. This is why the orientation page can describe Mittens by exhibiting its ten-leg cocone: those legs are exactly the generators of the relevant hom-sets." .

silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_14_kleisli_enrichment_pipeline_sections_02_enrichment_by_type_information_decomposition_step_6__step_o_01_is_set_enriched%3B_every_hom_set_is_explicitly_typed_and_
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Enrichment by type information means every arrow in the pipeline carries its sort declaration; the Yoneda profile of Mittens is the product of ten typed hom-sets; adding a new arrow requires explicit olog extension." .

silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_14_kleisli_enrichment_pipeline_sections_02_enrichment_by_type_information_olog_box__setenrichedpageolog01
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "SetEnrichedPageOlog01" .

silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_14_kleisli_enrichment_pipeline_sections_02_enrichment_by_type_information_yoneda_hom_leg_1
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "EnrichmentLegAboutVetRecord" ;
    rdfs:label "EnrichmentLegAboutVetRecordExample" ;
    silm:hasExample "In 'EnrichmentLegAboutVetRecord', the typed legs of the Yoneda hom-profile are witnessed by concrete Mittens-domain arrows. For example, JoC §6.18: Hom(VetRecord77, Mittens) = {about} is the Set-enriched hom-object; the single element \"about\" is the typed arrow from the vet record to Mittens." .

silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_14_kleisli_enrichment_pipeline_sections_02_enrichment_by_type_information_yoneda_hom_leg_2
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "EnrichmentLegLambdaCls" ;
    rdfs:label "EnrichmentLegLambdaClsExample" ;
    silm:hasExample "In 'EnrichmentLegLambdaCls', the typed legs of the Yoneda hom-profile are witnessed by concrete Mittens-domain arrows. For example, JoC §6.18 (representability) plus JoC §3 (Set-enriched categories): the singleton hom-set Hom_O_01(Mittens, DomesticCat) = {lambda_cls} is a one-element object of Set. The Set-enrichment makes the typed hom-set explicit and small. For the Mittens fixture, lambda_cls is the categorical statement \"Mittens is a DomesticCat\"." .

silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_14_kleisli_enrichment_pipeline_sections_02_enrichment_by_type_information_yoneda_hom_leg_3
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "EnrichmentLegMeasures" ;
    rdfs:label "EnrichmentLegMeasuresExample" ;
    silm:hasExample "In 'EnrichmentLegMeasures', the typed legs of the Yoneda hom-profile are witnessed by concrete Mittens-domain arrows. For example, JoC §6.18 plus the Set-enrichment of O_01: Hom_O_01(Measurement2024, Mittens) = {measures}. The 2024-11-01 body-mass measurement (4.1kg) measures the cat Mittens; the typed hom-set is small and named. The Set-enrichment guarantees that adding \"measured at a vet visit\" as a second arrow would require an explicit olog extension, not a fluent assumption." .

silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_14_kleisli_enrichment_pipeline_sections_02_enrichment_by_type_information_yoneda_hom_leg_4
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "EnrichmentLegLambdaTax" ;
    rdfs:label "EnrichmentLegLambdaTaxExample" ;
    silm:hasExample "In 'EnrichmentLegLambdaTax', the typed legs of the Yoneda hom-profile are witnessed by concrete Mittens-domain arrows. For example, JoC §6.18 plus the taxonomy-as-source-leg discipline: Hom_O_01(Mittens, TaxRow_TSN_183798) = {lambda_tax}. The arrow connects Mittens to the ITIS row for Felis catus (TSN 183798); it is a typed cocone leg, NOT an identification. The hom-set being singleton, plus the parallel singleton Hom_O_01(Mittens, DomesticCat) = {lambda_cls}, distinguishes classification from taxonomy." .

