    silm:hasLongDescription "The MittensColimitApex is The colimit apex of D_Mittens; target of iota_tsn but NOT equal to the TSN identifier. Mittens has ten typed legs; a database primary key has none of them. In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'Mittens', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .

silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_13_regression_test_suite_sections_02_probe_tsn_identity_concrete_anchor_3
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "ProbeTsnIdentityAnchorBareTsnNumeric" ;
    rdfs:label "ProbeTsnIdentityAnchorBareTsnNumericExample" ;
    silm:hasExample "In 'ProbeTsnIdentityAnchorBareTsnNumeric', the bare-symbol→anchor table grounds the abstract symbols in the Tartu-Animal-Clinic / Mittens-2026-05-18 domain story. For example, The bare numeric value 183798 considered apart from its containing ITIS row. In the R2 probe diagram, this is the dashed-red source node attempting a direct identity arrow to Mittens. It has no typed legs in O_01: no record leg, no measurement leg, no role leg; only a string/integer literal. The forbidden dashed arrow demonstrates that an identifier-as-field cannot replace an apex that requires a full ten-leg cocone.." .

