    rdfs:label "ProbeTsnIdentityAnchorBareTsnNumericAddlCircuitCorner" ;
    rdfs:label "ProbeTsnIdentityAnchorBareTsnNumericAddlDunbarLayer" ;
    rdfs:label "ProbeTsnIdentityAnchorBareTsnNumericAddlPaperKind" ;
    rdfs:label "urn:silmaril:entity#instances.papers.01_orientation.chapters.13_regression_test_suite.sections.02_probe_tsn_identity.concrete_anchor_3#baretsnnumeric183798" ;
    silm:hasAdditionalAttribute "base_topic:free monad" ;
    silm:hasAdditionalAttribute "circuit_corner:7" ;
    silm:hasAdditionalAttribute "dunbar_layer:0" ;
    silm:hasAdditionalAttribute "paper_kind:urn:silmaril:entity#papers.01_orientation" ;
    silm:hasLongDescription "The BareTsnNumeric183798 is The bare numeric value 183798 considered apart from its containing ITIS row. In the R2 probe diagram, this is the dashed-red source node attempting a direct identity arrow to Mittens. It has no typed legs in O_01: no record leg, no measurement leg, no role leg; only a string/integer literal. The forbidden dashed arrow demonstrates that an identifier-as-field cannot replace an apex that requires a full ten-leg cocone." .

silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_13_regression_test_suite_sections_02_probe_tsn_identity_decomposition_step_1__step_tsn_183798
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "TSN 183798 is the primary key for Felis catus in the ITIS relational database; it is a numeric identifier, not the cat itself." .

silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_13_regression_test_suite_sections_02_probe_tsn_identity_decomposition_step_2__step_iota_tsn__taxrow_tsn183798__%3E_mittens
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "The identification arrow iota_tsn goes FROM the ITIS row (source) TO the cat Mittens (target). The source is the row; the target is the apex. The TSN number is a field of the source, not the target." .

silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_13_regression_test_suite_sections_02_probe_tsn_identity_decomposition_step_3__step_joc_%C2%A73_1__objects_and_arrows_are_distinct_entities_in_a_category
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Joy of Cats §3.1 distinguishes objects (nodes) from arrows (morphisms). The TSN identifier labels the source object TaxRow_TSN183798; iota_tsn is the arrow; Mittens is the target object. These are three distinct categorical entities." .

silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_13_regression_test_suite_sections_02_probe_tsn_identity_decomposition_step_4__step_iota_tsn_loop_refutation__if_tsn_183798_%3D_mittens__then_iota
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "If TSN 183798 = Mittens, then the identification arrow iota_tsn would be a loop from Mittens to itself. But a loop is an endomorphism; it says nothing about the cat — it is a self-referential tautology. The olog structure distinguishes a domestic cat from a database row precisely because they have different types." .

silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_13_regression_test_suite_sections_02_probe_tsn_identity_decomposition_step_5__step_y%5Ein_mittens_%21%3D_y%5Ein_taxrow
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "By Yoneda, Mittens is determined by its full incoming/outgoing profile. Mittens has ten typed legs (record, identifier, quality, measurement, role, process, validation, trace, classification, taxonomy). TaxRow_TSN183798 has one outgoing arrow (iota_tsn into Mittens) and no other legs. The profiles differ; the objects differ." .

silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_13_regression_test_suite_sections_02_probe_tsn_identity_decomposition_step_6__step_probe_r2_holds
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "The TSN identifier is the source of a typed identification arrow, never the apex itself; the probe holds because the identifier is a field of the source node, not the colimit apex." .

silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_13_regression_test_suite_sections_02_probe_tsn_identity_olog_box__tsnidentityprober2
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "TsnIdentityProbeR2" .

