silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_15_witness_traceability_sections_02_witness_chain_protocol_concrete_anchor_1%23cannon_cheese_md
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "WitnessChainAnchorFileOnDiskAddlBaseTopic" ;
    rdfs:label "WitnessChainAnchorFileOnDiskAddlCircuitCorner" ;
    rdfs:label "WitnessChainAnchorFileOnDiskAddlDunbarLayer" ;
    rdfs:label "WitnessChainAnchorFileOnDiskAddlPaperKind" ;
    rdfs:label "urn:silmaril:entity#instances.papers.01_orientation.chapters.15_witness_traceability.sections.02_witness_chain_protocol.concrete_anchor_1#cannon_cheese.md" ;
    silm:hasAdditionalAttribute "base_topic:free monad" ;
    silm:hasAdditionalAttribute "circuit_corner:2" ;
    silm:hasAdditionalAttribute "dunbar_layer:0" ;
    silm:hasAdditionalAttribute "paper_kind:urn:silmaril:entity#papers.01_orientation" ;
    silm:hasLongDescription "The cannon/cheese.md is cannon/cheese.md is the source file for the cheese witness in the orientation entry. It is the leftmost node in the witness chain protocol diagram. The locate gate confirms it exists on disk; without this confirmation, the witness chain cannot start." .

silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_15_witness_traceability_sections_02_witness_chain_protocol_concrete_anchor_2
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "WitnessChainAnchorVerbatim" .

silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_15_witness_traceability_sections_02_witness_chain_protocol_concrete_anchor_2%23cheese_md_line_5__%22rational_mastery%22
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "WitnessChainAnchorVerbatimAddlBaseTopic" ;
    rdfs:label "WitnessChainAnchorVerbatimAddlCircuitCorner" ;
    rdfs:label "WitnessChainAnchorVerbatimAddlDunbarLayer" ;
    rdfs:label "WitnessChainAnchorVerbatimAddlPaperKind" ;
    rdfs:label "urn:silmaril:entity#instances.papers.01_orientation.chapters.15_witness_traceability.sections.02_witness_chain_protocol.concrete_anchor_2#cheese.md_line_5__\"rational_mastery\"" ;
    silm:hasAdditionalAttribute "base_topic:free monad" ;
    silm:hasAdditionalAttribute "circuit_corner:4" ;
    silm:hasAdditionalAttribute "dunbar_layer:0" ;
    silm:hasAdditionalAttribute "paper_kind:urn:silmaril:entity#papers.01_orientation" ;
    silm:hasLongDescription "The cheese.md line 5: \"rational mastery\" is \"rational mastery\" is the verbatim text from cannon/cheese.md line 5. It is the output of the extract gate. No paraphrase, no summary; the exact characters from the file. The Verbatim node is the third in the chain (SourceFile -> LineRange -> Verbatim -> LocalKey -> Witness). The extract gate produces this node; the key gate then assigns a local citation key to it." .

silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_15_witness_traceability_sections_02_witness_chain_protocol_decomposition_step_1__step_locate%3B_extract%3B_key%3B_cite_four_sequential_gates
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "The four gates are: locate (find the file on disk), extract (copy the relevant lines verbatim), key (assign a local citation key to the verbatim quote), cite (wrap as a Kleisli witness term in Free(Sigma)). Each gate is a named operation with a specific input and output." .

silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_15_witness_traceability_sections_02_witness_chain_protocol_decomposition_step_2__step_extract__verbatim_copy%3B_paraphrase__marked_alternative_with_
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "The extract gate has two modes: verbatim (default) and marked paraphrase (allowed only with explicit label, original key, and force-preservation). Verbatim extraction copies the exact text character-by-character. Marked paraphrase is allowed when labeled as interpretation_kind=source-leg-with-paraphrase-note. Unmarked paraphrase presented as verbatim is source-lying." .

silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_15_witness_traceability_sections_02_witness_chain_protocol_decomposition_step_3__step_joc_%C2%A715_1_factorization__source_is_file_on_disk%3B_target_is_l
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Joy of Cats §15.1 says every morphism in a factorization system has a declared source and target. In the witness chain, the source is the file on disk; the target is the local key. The four gates are the factored morphisms: locate goes source->LineRange; extract goes LineRange->VerbatimQuote; key goes VerbatimQuote->LocalKey. The factorization system license guarantees each gate is a named step with declared endpoints." .

silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_15_witness_traceability_sections_02_witness_chain_protocol_decomposition_step_4__step_cheese_md_witness__locate%3Dcannon_cheese_md%3B_extract%3Dline5%22ra
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "The cheese.md witness is traced through all four gates: (1) locate finds cannon/cheese.md on disk; (2) extract copies line 5 verbatim as \"rational mastery\" and line 11 as \"category weaponization\"; (3) key assigns the local citation key local-cannon-cheese-leary-alpert-witness-2026; (4) cite wraps as eta_Witness(cheese-l5) in Free(Sigma). All four gates pass; witness is traceable." .

silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_15_witness_traceability_sections_02_witness_chain_protocol_decomposition_step_5__step_traceable_iff__locate_o_extract_o_key_o_cite_%3D_valid_natural
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "By Yoneda, the chain protocol is traceable because every step is a natural transformation from the witness incoming profile (source file) to its outgoing profile (typed claims it supports). A chain that skips a step breaks the natural transformation. The dashed red shortcut from SourceFile to Witness (bypassing extract, key, cite) is not a natural transformation; it is a short-circuit that produces an untracked witness." .

silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_15_witness_traceability_sections_02_witness_chain_protocol_decomposition_step_6__step_witnesschain_holds
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "The four-gate protocol is complete; any skip produces an untracked witness; the result is either a refusal-mode flag or a swarmFlag adjacent to the claim. Verbatim is the default extraction mode; marked paraphrase is allowed when force-preserving and labeled." .

silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_15_witness_traceability_sections_02_witness_chain_protocol_olog_box__witnesschainprotocol__file__%3E_linerange__%3E_verbatim__%3E_local
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "WitnessChainProtocol: File -> LineRange -> Verbatim -> LocalKey -> Witness" .

