silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_14_kleisli_enrichment_pipeline_sections_03_cite_as_kleisli_arrow_decomposition_step_1__step_cite__source__%3E_freesigmawitness
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "The cite Kleisli arrow has domain Source (a source identifier: file path, DOI, or local key) and codomain Free(Sigma)(Witness). It produces a free-monad term of sort Witness without interpretation." .

silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_14_kleisli_enrichment_pipeline_sections_03_cite_as_kleisli_arrow_decomposition_step_2__step_eta_witnesskey__wraps_key_in_free_monad_without_interpretation
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "The unit embedding eta_Witness wraps the source key into a free-monad term of sort Witness. This is the smallest free term of sort Witness: it carries the key as a reference, not an interpretation." .

silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_14_kleisli_enrichment_pipeline_sections_03_cite_as_kleisli_arrow_decomposition_step_3__step_joc_%C2%A720_1__eta_b__b__%3E_tb_is_the_unit_of_the_monad
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "JoC §20.1 defines the unit eta_B: B -> T(B) as an embedding. Applying eta_Witness to a source key produces the smallest free term of sort Witness. The monad axiom eta bind f = f confirms cite then type = type directly." .

silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_14_kleisli_enrichment_pipeline_sections_03_cite_as_kleisli_arrow_decomposition_step_4__step_citemittensvetrecord77_%3D_eta_witnessmittensvetrecord77
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "The Mittens fixture key is mittensVetRecord77. cite(mittensVetRecord77) = eta_Witness(mittensVetRecord77): a free term that stands for the veterinary record witness before any interpretation." .

silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_14_kleisli_enrichment_pipeline_sections_03_cite_as_kleisli_arrow_decomposition_step_5__step_y%5Ein_profile_of_eta_witnessmittensvetrecord77_inherited_from
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "By Yoneda naturality, the profile of the unit term eta_Witness(mittensVetRecord77) is inherited from the Yoneda embedding of Witness into the Kleisli category. The terms profile is determined by how it maps into Mittens under the type and glue arrows." .

silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_14_kleisli_enrichment_pipeline_sections_03_cite_as_kleisli_arrow_decomposition_step_6__step_cite_%3D_unit_embedding%3B_records_provenance%3B_defers_interpretation
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "The cite Kleisli arrow is the unit embedding; it adds no interpretation; it tracks the source key as a free-monad term; downstream Kleisli steps (type, glue) produce claims." .

