    silm:hasAdditionalAttribute "paper_kind:urn:silmaril:entity#papers.01_orientation" ;
    silm:hasLongDescription "The cannon/cat/joy_of_cats.md is cannon/cat/joy_of_cats.md is the witness_path value in the joc620 ledger row. It is the leftmost source node in the ledger row anatomy diagram. Together with witness_line_range (2340-2360) and verbatim_quote, it constitutes the three-field traceability core that the locate+extract phase must produce." .

silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_15_witness_traceability_sections_03_ledger_row_anatomy_concrete_anchor_2
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "LedgerRowAnchorEditTarget" .

silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_15_witness_traceability_sections_03_ledger_row_anatomy_concrete_anchor_2%23sections_01_thesis_tex
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "LedgerRowAnchorEditTargetAddlBaseTopic" ;
    rdfs:label "LedgerRowAnchorEditTargetAddlCircuitCorner" ;
    rdfs:label "LedgerRowAnchorEditTargetAddlDunbarLayer" ;
    rdfs:label "LedgerRowAnchorEditTargetAddlPaperKind" ;
    rdfs:label "urn:silmaril:entity#instances.papers.01_orientation.chapters.15_witness_traceability.sections.03_ledger_row_anatomy.concrete_anchor_2#sections_01_thesis.tex" ;
    silm:hasAdditionalAttribute "base_topic:free monad" ;
    silm:hasAdditionalAttribute "circuit_corner:7" ;
    silm:hasAdditionalAttribute "dunbar_layer:0" ;
    silm:hasAdditionalAttribute "paper_kind:urn:silmaril:entity#papers.01_orientation" ;
    silm:hasLongDescription "The sections/01_thesis.tex is sections/01_thesis.tex is the edit_target value in the joc620 ledger row. It is the rightmost target node in the ledger row anatomy diagram. The typed morphism from the joc620 witness on disk terminates here. The weaver verifies the edit_diff_sha field by byte-checking the diff hunk against this file at Tier 4." .

silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_15_witness_traceability_sections_03_ledger_row_anatomy_decomposition_step_1__step_anchor%3B_witness_path%3B_witness_line_range%3B_interpretation_kin
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "The ledger has eight named columns: anchor (which section the claim belongs to), witness_path (file on disk), witness_line_range (specific lines), interpretation_kind (source-leg, negative-regression, etc.), verbatim_quote (exact text), validation_law (which rule governs the claim), edit_target (which paper section to edit), edit_diff_sha (SHA of the diff hunk)." .

silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_15_witness_traceability_sections_03_ledger_row_anatomy_decomposition_step_2__step_locate%2Bextract_phase__anchor_%2B_witness_path_%2B_witness_line_r
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "The anchor column names the section the claim belongs to. The witness_path and witness_line_range columns together constitute the locate phase. The verbatim_quote column is the output of the extract phase. Together, these four columns are the traceability core of the ledger row, corresponding to the first three fields of the witness object: path(w), lines(w), quote(w)." .

silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_15_witness_traceability_sections_03_ledger_row_anatomy_decomposition_step_3__step_joc_%C2%A73_1_morphism__named_source_object_%2B_named_target_object
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Joy of Cats §3.1 requires that a morphism have a named source object and a named target object. In the ledger, the source is the witness at the named path and line range; the target is the edited paper section at the named edit_target. The ledger row is a typed morphism: source = witness on disk, target = claim in paper section." .

silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_15_witness_traceability_sections_03_ledger_row_anatomy_decomposition_step_4__step_joc620_ledger_row__anchor%3D01_thesis%3B_path%3Dcannon_cat_joy_of_
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "The joc620 row is the complete 8-column ledger entry for the Yoneda lemma claim in the orientation thesis section. Anchor points to 01_thesis; witness_path and lines point to the Joy of Cats file; interpretation_kind is source-leg (positive claim); verbatim_quote is the exact theorem statement; validation_law is the diagram_sous resolute agent §5.2; edit_target is the thesis section tex file; edit_diff_sha tracks the hunk." .

silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_15_witness_traceability_sections_03_ledger_row_anatomy_decomposition_step_5__step_y%5Einrow_%3D_source_witness_at_path%2Blines%3B_y%5Eoutrow_%3D_typed_cla
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "The Yoneda profile of a ledger row: the incoming arrows are the source witness and the validation law; the outgoing arrows are the typed claim in the edit target. The row is a traceable path from source to claim. The weaver verifies the path by checking both endpoints byte-for-byte: the source exists at path+lines, and the edit_diff_sha matches the edit_target." .

silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_15_witness_traceability_sections_03_ledger_row_anatomy_decomposition_step_6__step_ledgerrow_holds__typed_morphism_with_8_accountability_fields
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "The ledger row is the accountability atom of the orientation entry; each row is a typed morphism from a source file to a paper section; the weaver verifies every row byte-for-byte in Tier 4." .

silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_15_witness_traceability_sections_03_ledger_row_anatomy_olog_box__ledgerrow__8_column_typed_morphism_source%3Dwitness_on_disk__t
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "LedgerRow: 8-column typed morphism (source=witness on disk, target=claim in paper section)" .

