    rdfs:label "urn:silmaril:entity#instances.papers.01_orientation.chapters.13_regression_test_suite.sections.03_probe_domesticcat_collapse.concrete_anchor_4#nonequalitywitnesscell" ;
    silm:hasAdditionalAttribute "base_topic:free monad" ;
    silm:hasAdditionalAttribute "circuit_corner:5" ;
    silm:hasAdditionalAttribute "dunbar_layer:0" ;
    silm:hasAdditionalAttribute "paper_kind:urn:silmaril:entity#papers.01_orientation" ;
    silm:hasLongDescription "The NonEqualityWitnessCell is The blank cell in the upper-right of the R3 tikzcd grid is not decorative: it is the diagrammatic carrier of the non-equality DomesticCat != TaxRow_TSN183798. Were the cell filled with an identification arrow, the probe would FAIL. The intentional emptiness records that the classification node (DomesticCat) and the taxonomy-source node (TaxRow_TSN183798 for Mittens, the Silver Spring resident cat owned by Mrs. Henderson) sit on opposite sides of the colimit apex Mittens and are connected only through Mittens, never directly. This is the geometric statement of probe R3." .

silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_13_regression_test_suite_sections_03_probe_domesticcat_collapse_decomposition_step_1__step_domesticcat
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "DomesticCat is the classification sort in O_01: the target of the outgoing arrow lambda_cls from Mittens. It carries the \"is a domestic cat\" predicate." .

silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_13_regression_test_suite_sections_03_probe_domesticcat_collapse_decomposition_step_2__step_iota_tsn__taxrow_tsn183798__%3E_mittens_inward_vs_lambda_cls__
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "The taxonomy-source node TaxRow_TSN183798 carries iota_tsn (inward to Mittens); the classification node DomesticCat carries lambda_cls (outward from Mittens). These arrows point in opposite directions through the apex." .

silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_13_regression_test_suite_sections_03_probe_domesticcat_collapse_decomposition_step_3__step_joc_%C2%A711_1__a_diagram_is_a_functor%3B_objects_at_distinct_index
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Joy of Cats §11.1: a diagram is a functor from an index category into C; objects at different positions in the index are mapped to distinct objects in C (unless explicitly equated). DomesticCat and TaxRow_TSN183798 are at different positions in J_Mittens." .

silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_13_regression_test_suite_sections_03_probe_domesticcat_collapse_decomposition_step_4__step_domesticcat_%3D_type%3B_taxrow_tsn183798_%3D_database_row_%E2%80%94_differ
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "If DomesticCat equalled any catus row, then lambda_cls (from Mittens to DomesticCat) would target a taxon-table row. But a classification is a type predicate; a database row is a data record. A classification arrow cannot target a data row without collapsing the type/instance distinction." .

silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_13_regression_test_suite_sections_03_probe_domesticcat_collapse_decomposition_step_5__step_homdomesticcat___is_not_naturally_iso_homtaxrow_tsn183798__
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "By Yoneda, DomesticCat and TaxRow have different outgoing arrow families. DomesticCat has arrows to other classification types (other species classifications); TaxRow has an inward identification arrow to Mittens and no outgoing classification arrows. The representable functors are not naturally isomorphic; the objects are distinct." .

silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_13_regression_test_suite_sections_03_probe_domesticcat_collapse_decomposition_step_6__step_probe_r3_holds
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "DomesticCat is the classification-type node (target of lambda_cls from Mittens); any catus taxon row is the taxonomy-source node (source of iota_tsn into Mittens); they sit on opposite sides of the apex and cannot be identified without collapsing the cocone." .

silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_13_regression_test_suite_sections_03_probe_domesticcat_collapse_olog_box__domesticcatcollapseprober3
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "DomesticCatCollapseProbeR3" .

silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_13_regression_test_suite_sections_03_probe_domesticcat_collapse_yoneda_hom_leg_1
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "ProbeDomesticCatCollapseLegLambdaCls" ;
    rdfs:label "ProbeDomesticCatCollapseLegLambdaClsExample" ;
    silm:hasExample "In 'ProbeDomesticCatCollapseLegLambdaCls', the typed legs of the Yoneda hom-profile are witnessed by concrete Mittens-domain arrows. For example, JoC §11.1: the diagram D_Mittens places DomesticCat at a distinct index position from TaxRow; lambda_cls is the outgoing classification leg." .

silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_13_regression_test_suite_sections_03_probe_domesticcat_collapse_yoneda_hom_leg_2
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "ProbeDomesticCatCollapseLegLambdaCls" ;
    rdfs:label "ProbeDomesticCatCollapseLegLambdaClsExample" ;
    silm:hasExample "In 'ProbeDomesticCatCollapseLegLambdaCls', the typed legs of the Yoneda hom-profile are witnessed by concrete Mittens-domain arrows. For example, JoC §11.1: A diagram D: J -> A in a category specifies which nodes are distinct objects. Here the classification leg lambda_cls: Mittens -> DomesticCat exits the apex outward into the classification sort, while the taxonomy identification arrow iota_tsn enters the apex from TaxRow_TSN183798. The two arrows live in disjoint hom-sets Hom(Mittens, DomesticCat) and Hom(TaxRow, Mittens) which cannot be identified without collapsing the cocone to a loop. This separation is the probe-R3 invariant." .

