    silm:hasLongDescription "The Hom_{O_01}(catus, Mittens) = empty is Hom_{O_01}(catus, Mittens) = empty is the claim produced by the negative witness gippidy00_R1 flowing through type -> TypedLeg_bot -> gate_refuse. This empty hom-set is the target node of the negative witness diagram. It is as load-bearing as a positive hom-set claim: it prevents the catus-Mittens identity collapse." .

silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_15_witness_traceability_sections_04_negative_witnesses_concrete_anchor_3
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "NegativeWitnessAnchorEmptyHomSet" ;
    rdfs:label "NegativeWitnessAnchorEmptyHomSetExample" ;
    silm:hasExample "In 'NegativeWitnessAnchorEmptyHomSet', the bare-symbol→anchor table grounds the abstract symbols in the Tartu-Animal-Clinic / Mittens-2026-05-18 domain story. For example, EmptyHomSet is the terminus of the gate_refuse arrow in the negative-witness chain. For the catus-collision probe, the empty hom-set is Hom_O_01(catus, Mittens) = empty: there is no admitted arrow from a bare catus row to the concrete cat Mittens. The negative witness from gippidy00 lines 97-105 (collision-list) supports this empty hom-set by enumerating the candidates that fail (bare catus, TSN 183798 alone, any catus row) and exhibiting why each cannot be Mittens.." .

