    silm:hasAdditionalAttribute "circuit_corner:2" ;
    silm:hasAdditionalAttribute "dunbar_layer:0" ;
    silm:hasAdditionalAttribute "paper_kind:urn:silmaril:entity#papers.01_orientation" ;
    silm:hasLongDescription "The GeometricGapForRefusedShortcut is The empty cells in the lower row between NegativeWitness_lower and the target column carry the geometric distance the not-exists direct arrow must visibly cross. For the catus-collision case, these cells record that the shortcut bypasses BOTH the type step (no olog sort assignment) AND the gate_refuse step (no admission predicate fired). The visual reach of the arrow from row 2 up to EmptyHomSet is what makes the negative-regression visibly refused. Removing the gap would collapse the shortcut into a short side-arrow and lose its semantic content." .

silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_15_witness_traceability_sections_04_negative_witnesses_decomposition_step_1__step_hom_o_01a__b_%3D_empty_negative_regression_claim
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "The symbol Hom-subscript-O_01 of A comma B equals the empty set. This is a statement about the page olog: there is no arrow from object A to object B in O_01. This is a typed claim, just as a positive claim says Hom(A,B) is non-empty. A negative witness provides the source evidence for this empty-hom-set claim." .

silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_15_witness_traceability_sections_04_negative_witnesses_decomposition_step_2__step_typenegativewitness_%3D_typedleg_bot%3B_gate_refusetypedleg_bot_
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "The type operation assigns a NegativeWitness the bottom typed leg (TypedLeg_bot). The gate_refuse operation then converts TypedLeg_bot into the empty hom-set claim. This is different from a positive witness where type assigns a concrete TypedLeg and admit produces a typed leg for the cocone. A negative witness types as bot and the gate refuses, producing the empty hom-set assertion." .

silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_15_witness_traceability_sections_04_negative_witnesses_decomposition_step_3__step_joc_%C2%A76_20_yoneda_embedding__full_and_faithful%3B_two_objects_i
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Joy of Cats §6.20 states that the Yoneda embedding is full and faithful: two objects are isomorphic exactly when their representable functors are naturally isomorphic. Showing that catus has no representable functor isomorphic to Mittens is a legitimate categorical claim. The negative witness (gippidy00 collision list) provides the evidence that Hom(catus, Mittens) is empty and thus no such natural isomorphism exists." .

silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_15_witness_traceability_sections_04_negative_witnesses_decomposition_step_4__step_gippidy00_r1_negative_witness__path%3Drebuttal_round00_gippidy
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "The negative witness for probe R1 is: path=rebuttal/round00/gippidy00.md, witness_line_range=97-105, interpretation_kind=negative-regression. The verbatim quote at those lines lists the collision candidates (multiple catus rows) and argues no single catus row identifies Mittens. This ledger row records that Hom_{O_01}(catus, Mittens) = empty." .

silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_15_witness_traceability_sections_04_negative_witnesses_decomposition_step_5__step_y_stability__homcatus__mittens_%3D_empty_now_%3D%3E_homcatus__mitt
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "By Yoneda, a negative-regression claim is stable: if Hom(catus, Mittens) is empty now, the naturality of the profile transformation says it remains empty unless a new arrow from catus to Mittens is explicitly added to O_01. No future agent can silently re-introduce the catus-Mittens identity collapse; they would have to add an explicit arrow, which would fire the regression test R1." .

silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_15_witness_traceability_sections_04_negative_witnesses_decomposition_step_6__step_negativewitness_holds__load_bearing_olog_objects_preventing_
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Negative witnesses are load-bearing olog objects; they prevent silent regression by keeping the empty-hom-set claims visible in the witnesses ledger; removing a negative witness row would allow future agents to silently re-introduce the forbidden collapse." .

