    silm:hasAdditionalAttribute "paper_kind:urn:silmaril:entity#papers.01_orientation" ;
    silm:hasLongDescription "The TypedNodeProfileClaim is TypedNode is the third node in the R4 absorption pipeline. For the running fixture, the local witness for the GPT phrase \"Mittens is the colimit of its observable profile\" is typed by the Node-or-Arrow gate as a ProfileClaim node in the page olog O_01. Only after this typing step does the witness gain a sort declaration and become eligible for the glue step that contributes a leg into D_Mittens." .

silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_13_regression_test_suite_sections_04_probe_generated_authority_concrete_anchor_5
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "ProbeGeneratedAuthorityAnchorMittens" ;
    rdfs:label "ProbeGeneratedAuthorityAnchorMittensExample" ;
    silm:hasExample "In 'ProbeGeneratedAuthorityAnchorMittens', the bare-symbol→anchor table grounds the abstract symbols in the Tartu-Animal-Clinic / Mittens-2026-05-18 domain story. For example, Mittens is the colimit apex colim(D_Mittens). In the R4 diagram it is the final upper-row node, reachable from GeneratedWitness only through the four-arrow chain cite -> type -> glue. The probe holds because no shortcut exists: the GPT-drafted phrase \"Mittens is the colimit of its observable profile\" cannot become a Mittens-leg without traversing cite, type, and glue. Mittens is the concrete individual (Mrs. Hendersons silver-furred cat with veterinary record 77, microchip ID 2018, weighed 4.1kg on 2024-11-01) and the apex of the typed cocone — not the GPT phrase.." .

