    rdfs:label "urn:silmaril:entity#instances.papers.01_orientation.chapters.13_regression_test_suite.sections.04_probe_generated_authority.concrete_anchor_6#forbiddenshortcutsourcecell" ;
    silm:hasAdditionalAttribute "base_topic:free monad" ;
    silm:hasAdditionalAttribute "circuit_corner:3" ;
    silm:hasAdditionalAttribute "dunbar_layer:0" ;
    silm:hasAdditionalAttribute "paper_kind:urn:silmaril:entity#papers.01_orientation" ;
    silm:hasLongDescription "The ForbiddenShortcutSourceCell is The second occurrence of GeneratedWitness in the lower row of the R4 diagram is the source of the dashed-red direct arrow. It is the same fixture (e.g., the GPT-drafted phrase \"Mittens is the colimit of its observable profile\") that appears in the upper row — but here its outgoing arrow attempts to bypass cite, type, and glue. The dashed-red rendering is the visual signal of forbidden-shortcut status; the lower-left cell exists in the diagram precisely to make this shortcut nameable and refusable. Without naming the forbidden route, the probe could not block it; without the lower cell, the probe diagram has no negative-regression target." .

silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_13_regression_test_suite_sections_04_probe_generated_authority_decomposition_step_1__step_generatedwitness
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "A GeneratedWitness is any material created or drafted without an external archival source: GPT-drafted phrases, locally-generated reformulations, material drawn from training data." .

silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_13_regression_test_suite_sections_04_probe_generated_authority_decomposition_step_2__step_cite__generatedwitness__%3E_localwitness_provenance_key_assignment
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "The cite operation is the first step: it assigns a local provenance key to the generated material. Only after key assignment does the material become a LocalWitness that can enter the typing gate." .

silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_13_regression_test_suite_sections_04_probe_generated_authority_decomposition_step_3__step_joc_%C2%A715_1__every_arrow_in_a_factorization_system_has_declare
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "JoC §15.1 (factorization structures for sources): every arrow in a factorization system must be exhibited as a morphism with a declared source object and a declared target object. A generated phrase has neither source nor target until it is typed." .

silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_13_regression_test_suite_sections_04_probe_generated_authority_decomposition_step_4__step_profileclaim__citejoc620__%3E_typeprofileclaim__%3E_gluemittens
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "The generated phrase \"Mittens is the colimit of its observable profile\" must pass four concrete gates: (a) cite assigns local key; (b) type classifies as ProfileClaim node in O_01; (c) gate validates the claim against JoC §11; (d) glue contributes the typed node to the cocone." .

silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_13_regression_test_suite_sections_04_probe_generated_authority_decomposition_step_5__step_ygeneratedwitness_%3D_empty_profile%3B_yprofileclaim_%3D_non_empty
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "By Yoneda, a claim becomes an encyclopedia object only when its representable profile is exhibited. A floating generated phrase has no arrows entering or leaving it in O_01; its profile is empty. After absorption, ProfileClaim has arrows from its witnesses and arrows into Mittens via glue." .

silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_13_regression_test_suite_sections_04_probe_generated_authority_decomposition_step_6__step_probe_r4_holds
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Generated fluency is draft material; admission requires the full absorption pipeline (cite, type, glue); direct promotion from generated text to olog claim is forbidden." .

