silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_14_kleisli_enrichment_pipeline_sections_04_type_as_kleisli_arrow_concrete_anchor_1%23witness_record
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "TypeKleisliAnchorWitnessRecordAddlBaseTopic" ;
    rdfs:label "TypeKleisliAnchorWitnessRecordAddlCircuitCorner" ;
    rdfs:label "TypeKleisliAnchorWitnessRecordAddlDunbarLayer" ;
    rdfs:label "TypeKleisliAnchorWitnessRecordAddlPaperKind" ;
    rdfs:label "urn:silmaril:entity#instances.papers.01_orientation.chapters.14_kleisli_enrichment_pipeline.sections.04_type_as_kleisli_arrow.concrete_anchor_1#witness_record" ;
    silm:hasAdditionalAttribute "base_topic:free monad" ;
    silm:hasAdditionalAttribute "circuit_corner:7" ;
    silm:hasAdditionalAttribute "dunbar_layer:0" ;
    silm:hasAdditionalAttribute "paper_kind:urn:silmaril:entity#papers.01_orientation" ;
    silm:hasLongDescription "The Witness_record is Witness_record is the Free(Sigma)-wrapped vet-record witness, produced by the cite step. It is the source of the gate arrow in the type diagram. After gate checks it (TypedNode_record), admit produces TypedLeg_record. The witness carries the vet-record provenance: file path, line range, verbatim quote, local key." .

silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_14_kleisli_enrichment_pipeline_sections_04_type_as_kleisli_arrow_concrete_anchor_2
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "TypeKleisliAnchorTypedLegRecord" ;
    rdfs:label "TypeKleisliAnchorTypedLegRecordExample" ;
    silm:hasExample "In 'TypeKleisliAnchorTypedLegRecord', the bare-symbol→anchor table grounds the abstract symbols in the Tartu-Animal-Clinic / Mittens-2026-05-18 domain story. For example, TypedLeg_record is the olog-object VetRecord77 viewed as a leg in the Mittens colimit diagram D_Mittens. After type^Kl assigns the \"record\" sort, this leg is available to the glue step which will wire it into the cocone via lambda_rec: TypedLeg_record -> Mittens.." .

silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_14_kleisli_enrichment_pipeline_sections_04_type_as_kleisli_arrow_concrete_anchor_2%23typedleg_record
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "TypeKleisliAnchorTypedLegRecordAddlBaseTopic" ;
    rdfs:label "TypeKleisliAnchorTypedLegRecordAddlCircuitCorner" ;
    rdfs:label "TypeKleisliAnchorTypedLegRecordAddlDunbarLayer" ;
    rdfs:label "TypeKleisliAnchorTypedLegRecordAddlPaperKind" ;
    rdfs:label "urn:silmaril:entity#instances.papers.01_orientation.chapters.14_kleisli_enrichment_pipeline.sections.04_type_as_kleisli_arrow.concrete_anchor_2#typedleg_record" ;
    silm:hasAdditionalAttribute "base_topic:free monad" ;
    silm:hasAdditionalAttribute "circuit_corner:7" ;
    silm:hasAdditionalAttribute "dunbar_layer:0" ;
    silm:hasAdditionalAttribute "paper_kind:urn:silmaril:entity#papers.01_orientation" ;
    silm:hasLongDescription "The TypedLeg_record is TypedLeg_record is the olog-object VetRecord77 viewed as a leg in the Mittens colimit diagram D_Mittens. After type^Kl assigns the \"record\" sort, this leg is available to the glue step which will wire it into the cocone via lambda_rec: TypedLeg_record -> Mittens." .

silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_14_kleisli_enrichment_pipeline_sections_04_type_as_kleisli_arrow_concrete_anchor_3
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "TypeKleisliAnchorGate" .

silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_14_kleisli_enrichment_pipeline_sections_04_type_as_kleisli_arrow_concrete_anchor_3%23gate
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "TypeKleisliAnchorGateAddlBaseTopic" ;
    rdfs:label "TypeKleisliAnchorGateAddlCircuitCorner" ;
    rdfs:label "TypeKleisliAnchorGateAddlDunbarLayer" ;
    rdfs:label "TypeKleisliAnchorGateAddlPaperKind" ;
    rdfs:label "urn:silmaril:entity#instances.papers.01_orientation.chapters.14_kleisli_enrichment_pipeline.sections.04_type_as_kleisli_arrow.concrete_anchor_3#gate" ;
    silm:hasAdditionalAttribute "base_topic:free monad" ;
    silm:hasAdditionalAttribute "circuit_corner:0" ;
    silm:hasAdditionalAttribute "dunbar_layer:0" ;
    silm:hasAdditionalAttribute "paper_kind:urn:silmaril:entity#papers.01_orientation" ;
    silm:hasLongDescription "The Gate is The Node-or-Arrow Gate is the intermediate object in the type factorization: Witness_record -> Gate -> TypedLeg_record. Gate checks whether the witness names a TypedNode (olog box), a TypedArrow (olog morphism), or neither (bot, refusal). For Witness_record: Gate = TypedNode_record. For an untyped witness like photoRecord2023: Gate = bot, chain halts." .

silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_14_kleisli_enrichment_pipeline_sections_04_type_as_kleisli_arrow_decomposition_step_1__step_type%5Ekl__witness__%3E_freesigmatypedleg
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "The symbol is called \"type-superscript-Kl\". The arrow goes FROM the object Witness TO the object Free-of-Sigma applied to TypedLeg. In the Kleisli category, this is the second pipeline arrow after cite." .

silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_14_kleisli_enrichment_pipeline_sections_04_type_as_kleisli_arrow_decomposition_step_2__step_gate%3B_admit%3B_type%5Ekl_%3D_admit_o_gate
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "gate is a predicate that asks: is this witness naming an olog object (TypedNode) or an olog arrow (TypedArrow) or neither (bot)? admit is the step that, when gate says yes, produces the TypedLeg. The full type operation = admit composed after gate." .

silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_14_kleisli_enrichment_pipeline_sections_04_type_as_kleisli_arrow_decomposition_step_3__step_joc_%C2%A715_1_factorization_systems
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Joy of Cats section 15.1 says: in a factorization system, every morphism factors uniquely as a right factor (the gate/epi) followed by a left factor (the admit/mono). The type step is one such factorization: gate is the epi part (checking sort), admit is the mono part (embedding into the typed leg)." .

silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_14_kleisli_enrichment_pipeline_sections_04_type_as_kleisli_arrow_decomposition_step_4__step_typemittensvetrecord77_%3D_typedleg_record%3B_typeitisrow183798_
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "The witness mittensVetRecord77 (from the vet record) gates as a TypedNode_record and is admitted as TypedLeg_record. The witness itisRow183798 (from the ITIS taxonomy row) gates as TypedNode_taxonomy and is admitted as TypedLeg_taxonomy. In both cases the witness names an olog object." .

silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_14_kleisli_enrichment_pipeline_sections_04_type_as_kleisli_arrow_decomposition_step_5__step_y%5Eintypedleg_record_%3D_admit_arrow_from_gate%3B_y%5Eouttypedleg_r
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "The Yoneda profile of TypedLeg_record has one incoming arrow: admit (the admission from the gate). It has one outgoing arrow: lambda_rec, the cocone leg from TypedLeg_record to the colimit apex Mittens. By Yoneda naturality, classifying the witness as a record leg fixes this profile and determines where glue will wire it in the cocone." .

silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_14_kleisli_enrichment_pipeline_sections_04_type_as_kleisli_arrow_decomposition_step_6__step_type%5Ekl_holds
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "The type Kleisli arrow assigns an olog sort to each witness by factoring through the Node-or-Arrow gate; the gate is the admissibility predicate that determines which node sorts are available; the result is a typed leg in O_01." .

