silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_14_kleisli_enrichment_pipeline_sections_04_type_as_kleisli_arrow_yoneda_hom_leg_3
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "TypeKleisliLegBendedTypeKl" ;
    rdfs:label "TypeKleisliLegBendedTypeKlExample" ;
    silm:hasExample "In 'TypeKleisliLegBendedTypeKl', the typed legs of the Yoneda hom-profile are witnessed by concrete Mittens-domain arrows. For example, JoC §20.1 plus JoC §15.1 (factorization structures): the bend-right arrow type^Kl: Witness_record -> TypedLeg_record displays the composite gate o admit as one Kleisli arrow in Kl(Free(Sigma)). The factorization makes the gate step visible WITHIN the type Kleisli arrow; the universal-property of the (E, M) factorization guarantees uniqueness. For the Mittens VetRecord77 fixture, gate accepts the witness (record sort recognized in O_01) and admit produces TypedLeg_record." .

