silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_14_kleisli_enrichment_pipeline_sections_05_glue_as_kleisli_arrow_concrete_anchor_5
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "GlueKleisliAnchorTypedLegClassification" ;
    rdfs:label "GlueKleisliAnchorTypedLegClassificationExample" ;
    silm:hasExample "In 'GlueKleisliAnchorTypedLegClassification', the bare-symbol→anchor table grounds the abstract symbols in the Tartu-Animal-Clinic / Mittens-2026-05-18 domain story. For example, TypedLeg_classification represents the classification source leg of D_Mittens as a typed olog object: it carries the membership arrow lambda_cls: Mittens -> DomesticCat. In the glue diagram it sits on the lower diagonal feeding into Mittens; it is a distinct olog object from the taxonomy leg above it, so the cocone receives classification and taxonomy as two separate compatible legs.." .

