silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_14_kleisli_enrichment_pipeline_sections_05_glue_as_kleisli_arrow_concrete_anchor_6
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "GlueKleisliAnchorEmptyTopRightCell" ;
    rdfs:label "GlueKleisliAnchorEmptyTopRightCellExample" ;
    silm:hasExample "In 'GlueKleisliAnchorEmptyTopRightCell', the bare-symbol→anchor table grounds the abstract symbols in the Tartu-Animal-Clinic / Mittens-2026-05-18 domain story. For example, The empty top-right cell of the glue diagram is intentional layout: it preserves the visual gap that lets the three TypedLeg arrows fan into Mittens without label collisions, and lets the competing-cocone-target arrow Mittens -> VetCarePlan77 read cleanly as the unique mediating u. For the Mittens fixture (cat with vet record 77, microchip 2018, body mass 4.1kg), the empty cell records that VetCarePlan77 is a separate object that COULD be a competing apex, not a duplicate Mittens. Removing this whitespace would crowd the universal-property statement into the apex column and obscure the canonical-apex claim.." .

silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_14_kleisli_enrichment_pipeline_sections_05_glue_as_kleisli_arrow_concrete_anchor_6%23gluediagramtoprightwhitespace
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "GlueKleisliAnchorEmptyTopRightCellAddlBaseTopic" ;
    rdfs:label "GlueKleisliAnchorEmptyTopRightCellAddlCircuitCorner" ;
    rdfs:label "GlueKleisliAnchorEmptyTopRightCellAddlDunbarLayer" ;
    rdfs:label "GlueKleisliAnchorEmptyTopRightCellAddlPaperKind" ;
    rdfs:label "urn:silmaril:entity#instances.papers.01_orientation.chapters.14_kleisli_enrichment_pipeline.sections.05_glue_as_kleisli_arrow.concrete_anchor_6#gluediagramtoprightwhitespace" ;
    silm:hasAdditionalAttribute "base_topic:free monad" ;
    silm:hasAdditionalAttribute "circuit_corner:5" ;
    silm:hasAdditionalAttribute "dunbar_layer:0" ;
    silm:hasAdditionalAttribute "paper_kind:urn:silmaril:entity#papers.01_orientation" ;
    silm:hasLongDescription "The GlueDiagramTopRightWhitespace is The empty top-right cell of the glue diagram is intentional layout: it preserves the visual gap that lets the three TypedLeg arrows fan into Mittens without label collisions, and lets the competing-cocone-target arrow Mittens -> VetCarePlan77 read cleanly as the unique mediating u. For the Mittens fixture (cat with vet record 77, microchip 2018, body mass 4.1kg), the empty cell records that VetCarePlan77 is a separate object that COULD be a competing apex, not a duplicate Mittens. Removing this whitespace would crowd the universal-property statement into the apex column and obscure the canonical-apex claim." .

silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_14_kleisli_enrichment_pipeline_sections_05_glue_as_kleisli_arrow_decomposition_step_1__step_glue__typedleg%5En__%3E_freesigmaapex
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "The symbol is called \"glue\". The arrow goes FROM a collection of n typed legs TO the Free(Sigma)-wrapped apex object. In the Kleisli category, this is the third and final pipeline arrow, after cite and type." .

silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_14_kleisli_enrichment_pipeline_sections_05_glue_as_kleisli_arrow_decomposition_step_2__step_cocone_compatibility__lambda_k_o_d_mittensalpha_%3D_lambda_j
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "The cocone compatibility law says: for every overlap arrow alpha from index object j to index object k in the diagram D_Mittens, the leg lambda_j equals lambda_k composed with D_Mittens(alpha). This law ensures all legs agree at overlaps. Glue checks this law before producing the colimit apex." .

silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_14_kleisli_enrichment_pipeline_sections_05_glue_as_kleisli_arrow_decomposition_step_3__step_joc_%C2%A711_3_universal_property_of_the_colimit
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Joy of Cats section 11.3 says: for every compatible cocone (C, (mu_j)), there is a unique mediating arrow u: Mittens -> C. This universal property is what makes the glue step produce the colimit rather than just any cocone apex. If you assembled all ten legs into something other than the true colimit, the mediating arrow u would not exist uniquely." .

silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_14_kleisli_enrichment_pipeline_sections_05_glue_as_kleisli_arrow_decomposition_step_4__step_gluevetrecord77__microchipid2018__bodymassquality__measureme
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "The ten typed legs for Mittens are: record=VetRecord77, identifier=MicrochipID2018, quality=BodyMassQuality, measurement=MeasurementEvent2024, role=HouseholdPetRole, process=VetVisit2024, validation=SHACLReport2024, trace=CatalogTrace2024, classification=DomesticCat, taxonomy=TaxRow_TSN183798. All ten must be typed and compatible. If measurement leg is missing, glue halts with a partial-cocone flag." .

silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_14_kleisli_enrichment_pipeline_sections_05_glue_as_kleisli_arrow_decomposition_step_5__step_y%5Einmittens_%3D_lambda_rec__lambda_id__lambda_qual__lambda_mea
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "The Yoneda profile of Mittens has ten incoming arrows (the ten cocone legs lambda_j) and one canonical outgoing arrow (the mediating map u to any competing cocone target). No competing cocone target VetCarePlan77 can replace Mittens as the colimit because VetCarePlan77 does not receive a unique mediating arrow from all other compatible cocones — only Mittens does." .

silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_14_kleisli_enrichment_pipeline_sections_05_glue_as_kleisli_arrow_decomposition_step_6__step_glue_holds
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Glue is the cocone-assembly step; ten compatible typed legs (paper-tier abstraction) are required; the colimit Mittens is the canonical apex by the universal property of the cocone." .

silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_14_kleisli_enrichment_pipeline_sections_05_glue_as_kleisli_arrow_olog_box__glue__typedleg%5En__%3E_freesigmaapex
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "glue: TypedLeg^n -> Free(Sigma)(Apex)" .

silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_14_kleisli_enrichment_pipeline_sections_05_glue_as_kleisli_arrow_yoneda_hom_leg_1
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "GlueKleisliLegLambdaRec" .

silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_14_kleisli_enrichment_pipeline_sections_05_glue_as_kleisli_arrow_yoneda_hom_leg_2
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "GlueKleisliLegUMediating" ;
    rdfs:label "GlueKleisliLegUMediatingExample" ;
    silm:hasExample "In 'GlueKleisliLegUMediating', the typed legs of the Yoneda hom-profile are witnessed by concrete Mittens-domain arrows. For example, JoC §11.3: For every compatible cocone (C, (mu_j)), there is a unique mediating arrow u: colim D -> C such that mu_j = u o lambda_j for all j. Here u: Mittens -> VetCarePlan77 satisfies mu_j = u o lambda_j for all ten legs j." .

silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_14_kleisli_enrichment_pipeline_sections_05_glue_as_kleisli_arrow_yoneda_hom_leg_3
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "GlueKleisliLegLambdaTax" ;
    rdfs:label "GlueKleisliLegLambdaTaxExample" ;
    silm:hasExample "In 'GlueKleisliLegLambdaTax', the typed legs of the Yoneda hom-profile are witnessed by concrete Mittens-domain arrows. For example, JoC §11: lambda_tax: TypedLeg_taxonomy -> Mittens is the taxonomy component of the colimit cocone for D_Mittens. For the Mittens fixture, it commits TaxRow_TSN_183798 (ITIS row for Felis catus, valid, rank Species) as the taxonomy source leg of the cat. The leg is preserved separately from lambda_cls (classification), keeping the negative-regression \"Mittens = catus\" blocked." .

silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_14_kleisli_enrichment_pipeline_sections_05_glue_as_kleisli_arrow_yoneda_hom_leg_4
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "GlueKleisliLegLambdaCls" ;
    rdfs:label "GlueKleisliLegLambdaClsExample" ;
    silm:hasExample "In 'GlueKleisliLegLambdaCls', the typed legs of the Yoneda hom-profile are witnessed by concrete Mittens-domain arrows. For example, JoC §11: lambda_cls: TypedLeg_classification -> Mittens is the classification component of the colimit cocone for D_Mittens. For the Mittens fixture, it commits the DomesticCat membership as the species-classification leg. The compatibility condition with the taxonomy leg (above) reads: the overlap arrow alpha: classification -> taxonomy in the index category, if present, must commute with lambda_cls and lambda_tax. Glue checks all such compatibilities before producing Mittens." .

