    silm:hasLongDescription "The TypedClaimMeasurementEvent2024 is TypedClaim is the third node in the R5 pipeline. For the Mittens fixture, the Witness object becomes the typed claim MeasurementEvent2024 carrying source=Mittens, quality=BodyMassQuality, value=4.1, unit=kg, date=2024-11-01. The typed sort enables the validate arrow but does not yet guarantee SHACL-shape compliance — the validate step has not run." .

silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_13_regression_test_suite_sections_05_probe_ungated_render_concrete_anchor_4
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "ProbeUngatedRenderAnchorValidatedClaim" ;
    rdfs:label "ProbeUngatedRenderAnchorValidatedClaimExample" ;
    silm:hasExample "In 'ProbeUngatedRenderAnchorValidatedClaim', the bare-symbol→anchor table grounds the abstract symbols in the Tartu-Animal-Clinic / Mittens-2026-05-18 domain story. For example, ValidatedClaim is the fourth node in the R5 pipeline. For the Mittens fixture, MeasurementEvent2024 passes the SHACL shape MeasurementEventShape (mass-must-be-positive, date-must-parse-as-ISO8601, quality-must-be-BodyMassQuality). Only after this validation can the render arrow fire on the claim; an unvalidated typed claim is still ungated for proof-surface rendering.." .

