    silm:hasAdditionalAttribute "paper_kind:urn:silmaril:entity#papers.01_orientation" ;
    silm:hasLongDescription "The UngatedRenderShortcutSource is The second SourcePhrase cell in the lower row of the R5 diagram is the source of the dashed-red \"ungated\" shortcut to RenderedDiagram. For the Mittens fixture this is the same string \"Mittens measured at 4.1kg on 2024-11-01\" — but here the agent attempts to render the string directly into a figure box without ingest, type, or validate. The duplicated cell exists to make this shortcut visually nameable; the dashed-red rendering signals refusal status." .

silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_13_regression_test_suite_sections_05_probe_ungated_render_concrete_anchor_7
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "ProbeUngatedRenderAnchorRowTwoEmptyCells" .

silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_13_regression_test_suite_sections_05_probe_ungated_render_concrete_anchor_7%23geometricgapforungatedshortcut
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "ProbeUngatedRenderAnchorRowTwoEmptyCellsAddlBaseTopic" ;
    rdfs:label "ProbeUngatedRenderAnchorRowTwoEmptyCellsAddlCircuitCorner" ;
    rdfs:label "ProbeUngatedRenderAnchorRowTwoEmptyCellsAddlDunbarLayer" ;
    rdfs:label "ProbeUngatedRenderAnchorRowTwoEmptyCellsAddlPaperKind" ;
    rdfs:label "urn:silmaril:entity#instances.papers.01_orientation.chapters.13_regression_test_suite.sections.05_probe_ungated_render.concrete_anchor_7#geometricgapforungatedshortcut" ;
    silm:hasAdditionalAttribute "base_topic:free monad" ;
    silm:hasAdditionalAttribute "circuit_corner:0" ;
    silm:hasAdditionalAttribute "dunbar_layer:0" ;
    silm:hasAdditionalAttribute "paper_kind:urn:silmaril:entity#papers.01_orientation" ;
    silm:hasLongDescription "The GeometricGapForUngatedShortcut is The blank cells in the lower row of the R5 tikzcd between SourcePhrase_lower and the trailing empty columns are intentional layout: they record the geometric distance that the dashed-red ungated arrow must cross. The visible reach of the forbidden shortcut from the lower row up to RenderedDiagram is what makes the negative-regression case readable. Were the cells filled, the shortcut would be a short side-arrow and would lose its rhetorical force as the rule-breaking long jump from raw source to proof surface. For the Mittens fixture, this is the visual representation that \"Mittens measured at 4.1kg on 2024-11-01\" -> rendered figure SKIPS ingest, type, AND validate — three named gates, three blank cells." .

silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_13_regression_test_suite_sections_05_probe_ungated_render_decomposition_step_1__step_rendereddiagram
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "RenderedDiagram is the target sort of the render functor in the page olog. A RenderedDiagram that carries proof status must have been produced by render(ValidatedClaim)." .

silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_13_regression_test_suite_sections_05_probe_ungated_render_decomposition_step_2__step_publish_%3D_render_o_validate_o_type_o_ingest
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "The render operation is the final functor in the publish factorization chain: publish = render composed with validate composed with type composed with ingest. The render functor is at the end; it sees only a ValidatedClaim as its source." .

silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_13_regression_test_suite_sections_05_probe_ungated_render_decomposition_step_3__step_joc_%C2%A713_5__a_functor_preserves_colimit_structure_only_when_s
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "JoC §13.5: a functor preserves the colimit structure only when source and target categories are correctly paired. A render functor applied to a pre-validation sort sees only the pre-validation category; the resulting diagram does not carry the validation legs of the ValidatedClaim category." .

silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_13_regression_test_suite_sections_05_probe_ungated_render_decomposition_step_4__step_measurementevent2024_ungated__figure_shows_%224_1_kg%22_but_has_
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "If the source phrase \"Mittens measured at 4.1 kg on 2024-11-01\" is rendered directly without typing MeasurementEvent2024 and validating via the SHACL shape, the figure shows a box labelled \"4.1 kg\" but has no admitted measurement leg in the page olog." .

silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_13_regression_test_suite_sections_05_probe_ungated_render_decomposition_step_5__step_yrendereddiagram_from_ungated_%21%3D_yrendereddiagram_from_validated
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "The profile of a rendered diagram should match the profile of the admitted claim. If the render bypasses the gate, the profiles differ: the reader traversing the Yoneda profile of the ungated figure finds the measurement leg missing; the profile of the admitted figure includes the measurement leg (MeasurementEvent2024 -> Mittens via measures)." .

silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_13_regression_test_suite_sections_05_probe_ungated_render_decomposition_step_6__step_probe_r5_holds_for_proof_surface_diagrams
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "The render functor admits only validated claims; an ungated proof-surface render produces a visual artefact, not a proof surface; schematic diagrams labelled as illustrative-only are outside the probe scope." .

